From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joinery Build <build@joinery.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:14:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(editor): start new projects from a playable starting
 point

Joinery-only, not meant for upstream: it reroutes Godot's new-project
dialog through the Joinery CLI.

The wizard's three steps become "What are you making?" (starting point
cards with a capture, name, folder and the game in one sentence),
"Features and apps" (a switch per feature with its reason when it can't be
used, requires and conflicts applied live, Steam's app ID and how players
connect inline, the apps behind one summary line with readiness and
Check again) and "Brief and art direction" (the brief's pitch and
audience, the art questions with References as their own section, and
the starting point's rules preset).

Everything shown comes from `joinery blueprints --json`, `tools --json`,
`bible --questions` and `brief --questions`, loaded on the worker thread.
project.godot is written before the steps run, because
`joinery game apply` merges the starting point's settings into it; the
creating page then copies the addon with its MIT licence, sets up git,
applies the starting point (downloading GodotSteam when Steam is on),
saves the apps, and writes the brief and the art bible.

The theme gains JoineryCard and JoinerySwitch, matching the addon.

Joinery-only start screen and setup flow, not intended for upstream.
